Z||000000||Gold-86SE||10-16-2000||06:02 PM||||<BR>I did a search, but did not find answers to my questions, so here they are.<P>I am going to be mating an 85 Iron Duke to an 84 4.10 4 speed tranny.<P>I was looking at the FS to see what they had and prices for it.<P>Now, here is my question - will the 85-86 4 SPEED HEAVY DUTY CLUTCH KIT" work in this application?  I ask because V6 is not specified, here is the link: <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=54002&variation=&aitem=10&mitem=18" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=54002&variation=&aitem=10&mitem=18</A> <P>Second, providing that this works, will a HD clutch be heavy and require a lot of left foot work?<P>Third, how long of a life will a HD clutch give me in this application?<P>The FS shows a clutch, pressure plate, throwout bearing, and alignment tool for just under what they are asking for the 85-86 HD clutch.  But, if the 85-86 HD clutch will work, I am leaning that direction.<P>I want a clutch that will last me, at minimum, 80k miles.  The 84 is not my performance machine, just my runabout.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.txconnect.com/home/rharris/signature-a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
